commit `1d0d702` (amend of `b43a746`), exactly one commit past checkpoint `f34d91d`, worktree clean, signature Good.\n\n## What the blocking finding actually was\n\nThe command-tag agreement in `internal/cliresult/client.go:readSuccess` was proven at **one** ordered pair. I reproduced both surviving narrowings at the reviewed head **before writing a line of test code**:\n\n| Mutant | Pre-fix | Post-fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `command != CommandDoctor` (control) | KILLED | KILLED |\n| `command != CommandList` | **SURVIVED** | KILLED |\n| `result.Command() != CommandTakeover` | **SURVIVED** (all 13 pkgs `ok`) | KILLED |\n\nThe sweep now drives every implemented tag against every other implemented tag's own emitted document — 306 ordered pairs, each required to refuse **with this guard's own sentence naming both tags**, so a pair settled by the version binding doesn't count as coverage of it. The 18 agreeing pairs must be admitted in the same loop; that's the control against a guard that refuses everything.\n\nThe bound is a ratio, not prose. All 1,936 ordered pairs over the 44 registered tags are classified: **18 admitted, 306 by this guard, 1,144 refused before stdout is read, 468 by the version binding.** For the 26 unimplemented tags the guard is never the enforcement — a measured class with a named earlier refusal behind it, not an assumption that nothing was bypassed.\n\n## Observation A extended, not just recorded\n\nThe reviewer measured the 4096-byte narrowing surviving on `axerror.requireCommonDataModel` and declined to block. **The identical narrowing on `documentSchema`'s copy in `cliresult` also survived** — same class, sibling reader, not in the review. Both are closed with conforming documents several times that size. One design note worth keeping: my first padding helper had *two* size sources, so narrowing either loop alone left the document large and the mutant read as equivalent. A size fixture needs one knob.\n\nObservation B (the `exitStatus`/`ExitCode()` equivalence) left alone as instructed.\n\n## Measured, with real exit codes\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | ---: |\n| `go build ./...` / `go vet ./...` | 0 / 0 |\n| `gofmt -l .` | no files |\n| `go test ./... -count=1` | 0, 13 packages |\n| `go test ./... -cover -count=1` | 0 — cliresult 95.5%, axerror 99.5%, unchanged |\n| `tracecheck` | 0 — `acceptance_cases=74`, `clauses_discharged=17/403`, unchanged |\n| Mutation harness (53 mutants) | 0 — 52 killed, 1 declared subsumed, 0 unexplained survivors, 36 narrowing |\n\nNo production code changed. Both new tests register against **existing** acceptance cases, so no coverage figure moved; each registration was probed by renaming its declaration and confirming `tracecheck` names the missing declaration ahead of the digest check.\n\nАхпер джан, одно предупреждение для ревьюера, записал его в notes: **`handoff` не строит CR**. Newest stored revision rev4 всё ещё указывает на pre-amend tree `2e893d0d`; актуальное дерево — `42898ceb`. Приложил `rework-r5-delta.patch` (7 файлов, 385/12) и `leaf-full-r5.patch`, читать надо их, а не сохранённый CR-патч.","ttft_ms":2059,"type":"result","duration_ms":1454905,"uuid":"8a42c915-4837-40ff-aeda-d3c209322027","ttft_stream_ms":1316,"time_to_request_ms":34,"queued_turn_count":0}
